<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nasir Khan I of Kalat</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1794</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Mir Nasir Khan I</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mir Nasir Khan I was Khan of Kalat from 1749 to 1794 and the most powerful ruler of the khanate. After a failed war in 1758 he accepted the overlordship of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmad-shah-abdali">Ahmad Shah Durrani</a> while keeping internal independence. He organised the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baloch">Baloch</a> and Brahui tribes into a confederacy with regular military contingents and an administration, and extended Kalat's rule over Makran and Las Bela to the coast.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nasir-khan-i-of-kalat.jpg" alt="Nasir Khan I of Kalat" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mostafameraji · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Street_football_in_Iran_%D9%81%D9%88%D8%AA%D8%A8%D8%A7%D9%84_%D8%AE%DB%8C%D8%A7%D8%A8%D8%A7%D9%86%DB%8C_(%DB%8C%D8%A7_%D8%B2%D9%85%DB%8C%D9%86_%D8%AE%D8%A7%DA%A9%DB%8C)_-_%DB%8C%D8%A7_(%DA%AF%D9%84_%DA%A9%D9%88%DA%86%DB%8C%DA%A9)_%D8%AF%D8%B1_%D8%A7%DB%8C%D8%B1%D8%A7%D9%86-_%D9%85%D9%86%D8%B7%D9%82%D9%87_%D8%AC%D9%86%D9%88%D8%A8_%DA%A9%D8%B1%D9%85%D8%A7%D9%86_05.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
